            "date": "2021-03-07T06:15:37Z"
          },
          "message": "Try fixing autoFocus again, and remove all rAF usage (#16)\n\nThis attempts to fix the problem with `autoFocus` by breaking out of React's Effect ordering and instead immediately disabling existing layers whenever a new layer is _about_ to be added (i.e., it runs inline with the component code, not in a callback to be run after the tree has been committed). Since `autoFocus` happens when the tree gets committed to the DOM, this should ensure that existing layers will not intercept that focus event.",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "4310bf11c407e3c0590c38b2b6122f1774a4881b",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/focus-layers/git/trees/4310bf11c407e3c0590c38b2b6122f1774a4881b"
          },
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/focus-layers/git/commits/37ab5d74bcd243ddff1b15c48e9501ec9ec6e0ca",
          "comment_count": 0,
          "verification": {
            "verified": true,
            "reason": "valid",
            "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJgRG+JCRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAAdHIIADbNWeS9ukRqrQYmAFge1tV1\nCUk3eD05grZ+Ec0miEtH8SPPJnx5ojFESg+WQC4Xp0dMpQLJGFDxRo3IEGCaY4vg\njhgCC87OFkk4DETysBawJJiNBb9zYqbwv7uAsoJs8VMOUQPZvJvoVyeYfy3HMhMF\nryUi8tahhl7Y0JJLySLSvjMrRydhkw98Ejc0IzURsx1mEbaQIIJsdTpQ1c4NJm4+\n6ht3k1eTKv4OAMzhSIdd5ij1PkOeSGLFnIiayslSbdeGzjWhM/FLmH4iGSTGEjcB\nIsk3xgAs5NFIUy2IS9fAWfwXd9/ioONxwOt/pvUMSnw7sfqnRxs9ouYCWTS158w=\n=62jL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
            "payload": "tree 4310bf11c407e3c0590c38b2b6122f1774a4881b\nparent 80241418b86069ee5c6e4e80ae10c7aa80049d52\nauthor Jon <jon.egeland@discordapp.com> 1615097737 -0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1615097737 -0800\n\nTry fixing autoFocus again, and remove all rAF usage (#16)\n\nThis attempts to fix the problem with `autoFocus` by breaking out of React's Effect ordering and instead immediately disabling existing layers whenever a new layer is _about_ to be added (i.e., it runs inline with the component code, not in a callback to be run after the tree has been committed). Since `autoFocus` happens when the tree gets committed to the DOM, this should ensure that existing layers will not intercept that focus event."
          }
        },
